<ecoSpold xmlns="http://www.EcoInvent.org/EcoSpold02">
  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="dee68439-5c53-59dc-b618-8bf5bf3aa9eb" activityNameId="546d0c5d-ac08-58ce-bdcc-05bc8b5ba8fc" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Production efforts, capacitors</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Production efforts, capacitors
Data are a rough estimation of the average production efforts over all types of capacitors. Data for auxillaries, energy, emissions and waste are taken from the Environmental report of a global producer as well as from two datasets out of an international LCI database. Infrastructure and transportation efforts are based on own assumptions. Updates were made in 2023, showing that 20% energy reduction is achieved; UUID: 913f85cb-31da-318d-ad0d-0e419e740cec
This module includes auxillary and energy consumption, emissions (air, water) and waste amounts, as well as an estimation of the efforts for transportation and of the infrastructure for the production of capacitors.
Location: Data from literature and one global producer – here representing the global situation.
Technology: average production of: formulation; build-up process; cutting; bisquing; Pre-Firing; Firing; Tumbling; Termination (SMT) resp. metallization; slitting; winding; metal spray; heat treatment; sawing; lead welding; epoxy filling (THT)
Time period: Unspecified
Production volume: 
Sampling: own estimation
Extrapolations: see Geography &amp; Technology
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_913f85cb-31da-318d-ad0d-0e419e740cec.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="f4808887-5a57-5892-975e-ba0565a93e23" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <shortname xml:lang="en">GLO</shortname>
        <comment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Location: Data from literature and one global producer – here representing the global situation.</text>
        </comment>
